// Ch7 B05 "The naming" (docs/kb/story/beats/act1_ch07.md §2 B05; decisions_log N-12). Played when
// Rhen comes down to the catch-pool's rim. Before each Tidecup match the two captains stand on the
// rim stones under the weeping column and each names one person the sea has taken. NO ONE PRESIDES:
// no Order official blesses or opens anything (ADR 0017 Ch7 watch). R03: the crowd falls silent from
// the pool outward until there is real silence (Audio: no music, no bed, only the column's weep).
// Ione Merrow (not Sabe: Oruvel's old diver has that name; M4-A2P-116 C5), Sorrin's captain, names her brother; the whole Bell answers with one word. R04, Tavi
// names the whole town; a long hold; the answer is louder and ragged at the edges because some
// people are crying. Asha says it quietly with them in the third gallery, Toma too, and Rhen in the
// water, looking up the column at the drop; if he lit his Pemakar boat for Oruvel, he says it a beat
// before anyone (a face cue, no extra line). "Up." is what you call to a diver who should be
// surfacing, and a score is bringing the float up; the game never says it is also the direction of
// the dead (bible §2). Played completely straight. R05: from inside the column looking down as the
// two sides swim up into it, the hand-off frame. The last op is the hand-off to the Reefball match
// (§5): `start_reefball tidecup_opening` (the Reefball agent's story-match id). The chapter flow reads
// it (if_event) and runs ch07.json's `reefball_match` beat.
title: ch07_naming
location: ch07/tamsule_bell_galleries
---
@letterbox on
@camera R03
@music silence fade=3.0
@wait 3.0
@sfx column_weep
@wait 1.5
Ione [neutral]: Aldo Merrow. My brother. #line:ch07_naming_001
@wait 1.0
Crowd [neutral]: Up. #line:ch07_naming_002 #tn:"The call to a diver who should be surfacing. One word, said low and together by ten thousand people."
@sfx crowd_up
@wait 2.0
@camera R04
@wait 1.5
Tavi [grief]: Oruvel. #line:ch07_naming_003
@wait 2.5
<<if $ch05_boat_for_oruvel>>
    @face rhen grief 0.5
<<endif>>
Crowd [grief]: Up. #line:ch07_naming_004 #tn:"The same answer, louder this time and ragged at the edges: some of the crowd are crying."
@sfx crowd_up vol=1.0
@face asha grief
@face toma grief
@anim rhen look_at drop
@wait 2.0
@camera R05
@wait 2.0
<<event start_reefball tidecup_opening>>
===
